---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { buildService } from '../lib/seo/organization';

const service = buildService(Astro.site!);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Services · Birch Design Lab"
  description="Custom software and custom websites for businesses that want to grow, designed, constructed, and cared for by one accountable craftsman."
>
  <JsonLd slot="head" data={service} />
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="smallcaps kicker">Services</p>
      <h1>Two things, done properly.</h1>
      <p class="subline">
        Same person designs it, builds it, and answers when you call. That's the whole model, twice.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="service">
      <h2>Custom software</h2>
      <p>
        Every business runs on a few things that never made it into any official system: the client list split across three phones, the schedule you're building from a paper calendar and a gut feeling, the order that gets tracked in a group text until someone loses it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We build the small, sturdy tool that replaces whichever one is costing you the most time. We can stay around to keep it running as the business grows past it.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="service">
      <h2>Custom websites</h2>
      <p>
        Your website is the first impression most customers will ever get. Whether that's deciding where to eat tonight, booking a charter, or comparing venues.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ours load fast, read clearly on any device, and are built around one question. What should they do next; call, book, order, walk in?
      </p>
      <p>
        Menus that update in minutes, not PDFs. Booking that keeps the reservation with you instead of a third-party app. Every site is designed and constructed by the same two hands, for the business it belongs to.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="process">
      <h2>How a project runs</h2>
      <ol class="steps" role="list">
        <li class="row">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true"></p>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Discovery</h3>
            <p>We meet, you talk, I take notes. No questionnaire, no workshop with a slide deck. You leave with a plain-language scope, not a pitch.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true"></p>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Build</h3>
            <p>You get a working link immediately. Access to the real build you can click through, not a mockup. Watch it evolve and fold in feedback throughout. No surprise reveal at the end.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true"></p>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Launch</h3>
            <p>Tested on multiple devices. Delivered with an owner's manual and a bow. Take it to anyone you choose afterwards or stick around.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <p class="num" aria-hidden="true"></p>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Care</h3>
            <p>Software is a living thing. We offer ongoing care so it stays fast, secure, and current as your business grows. It's yours either way.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section class="loud" data-reveal>
    <div class="wrap loud-inner">
      <p class="pull">Every project starts with a normal conversation.</p>
      <a class="cta-engraved" href="/contact">
        <span class="fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="lbl">Tell us about your project</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-5); max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .kicker { color: var(--accent); }
  .intro h1 { font-size: var(--text-3xl); margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .subline { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--mark-muted); margin-top: var(--space-3); }

  .service { padding-block: var(--space-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .service p { color: var(--mark-muted); margin-top: var(--space-3); }

  /* Process — display-serif numerals in a 7rem column. */
  .process { padding-block: var(--space-5) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: var(--space-4); counter-reset: step; }
  .row {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .row + .row { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .num {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    color: var(--accent); line-height: 1;
  }
  .num::before { content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero); }
  .step p { color: var(--mark-muted); margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  /* Phone: collapse the 7rem numeral column to single column (authored fresh —
     the kit's .process-row collapse rule was scaffolding, never ported). */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); }
  }

  /* Loud moment — closing CTA (.loud primitive in base.css). */
  .pull {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    line-height: 1.2; max-width: 40ch;
  }
  .loud .cta-engraved { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
